      "side": 1,
      "message": "No API should ever use both constants as possible return values. The value 0 is meant to symbolize success / true / supported / allowed. Unfortunately, the name \"SUCCESS\" isn\u0027t a clear return value for every function call. For function like isLeAudioSupported, a return value of \"SUCCESS\" isn\u0027t really clear. In these cases, we replace SUCCESS with FEATURE_SUPPORTED. The underlying value is kept the same, but it\u0027s just a clearer signal to the developer.",
